<title>THAILAND: Competition hits Thai Airways Q3 - analyst.</title>
<headline>Competition hits Thai Airways Q3 - analyst.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Analysts attributed a painful dive in Thai Airways International Plc third quarter profits on Friday to falling competitiveness in the global industry.</p>
<p>Mike Stead, head of Research at Union Securities in Bangkok, said the company had been losing ground to more efficient foreign airlines which have been more aggressive in offering new services to customers.</p>
<p>&quot;Thai is hampered by the fact that it is mainly controlled by the government. Political and military interests are hampering Thai,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
